    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d17-f1" n="1" xml:id="d17-f1-content">
                <p> NSC 20/4, “United States Objectives With Respect to the USSR To Counter Soviet
                    Threats to U.S. Security,” a report dated November 23, 1948, is printed in <ref
                        target="frus1948v01p2#pg_662">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1948, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, Part 2, p. 662</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f2" n="2" xml:id="d17-f2-content">
                <p> NSC 68, “United States Objectives and Programs for National Security,” April 14,
                    1950, and NSC 68/4, December 14, 1950, same title, are printed <ref
                        target="frus1950v01#pg_234">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, 1950, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >i</hi>, pp. 234</ref> and <ref target="frus1950v01#pg_467">467</ref>,
                    respectively. NSC 68/2, September 30, 1950, same title, is printed in part, <ref
                        target="frus1950v01#pg_400">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p. 400</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f3" n="3" xml:id="d17-f3-content">
                <p>See footnote 4, <ref target="#pg13">p. 13</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f4" n="4" xml:id="d17-f4-content">
                <p>The Senior Staff of the National Security Council consisted of Assistant
                    Secretary-level representatives nominated by the Departments of State, Defense,
                    and Treasury; the National Security Resources Board; the Central Intelligence
                    Agency; the Joint Chiefs of Staff; and the Office of Defense Mobilization. The
                    Executive Secretary of the NSC served as chairman. The Senior Staff, which met
                    approximately twice a week, constituted the principal staff arm of the
                    Council.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
